This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.

**MANDATORY: run graphify before Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash exploration** — for you and for every subagent you spawn, so include this rule in any subagent prompt that explores code. Do not skip it because the files are "already known" or because you are executing a plan; the graph surfaces cross-file and INFERRED edges that grep and Read cannot.

- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for a codebase or architecture question
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

Go straight to Read/Grep/Glob only when graphify has already oriented you and you need specific lines, or when `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist.

Prefer `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` over raw files when it exists. Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain are not enough. After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).
